    {
      "id": "alloy_system_1",
      "name": "BCC-base superalloy",
      "material_category": "superalloy",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "page": 1,
          "section": "Abstract",
          "quote": "Body-centered-cubic (BCC)-base superalloys primarily containing refractory elements have great potential as one kind of 'beyond Ni-base superalloy' materials",
          "table": null,
          "figure": null,
          "chunk_id": "1b6855b4033595e2:part:001"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "alloy_system_2",
      "name": "ferritic superalloy",
      "material_category": "Fe-based superalloy",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "page": 1,
          "section": "Introduction",
          "quote": "The coherent precipitation of ordered B2 phase (NiAl-type) into disordered body-centered-cubic (BCC) solid solution has given rise to ferritic superalloys in Fe-Cr-Ni-Al-based systems",
          "table": null,
          "figure": null,
          "chunk_id": "1b6855b4033595e2:part:001"
        },
        {
          "page": 5,
          "section": null,
          "quote": "Compared with commercial BCC heat-resistant steels, the ferritic superalloys exhibit outstanding creep resistance at 973 K.",
          "table": null,
          "figure": null,
          "chunk_id": "1b6855b4033595e2:part:002"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "alloy_system_3",
      "name": "refractory superalloy",
      "material_category": "refractory high-entropy alloy",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "page": 1,
          "section": "Introduction",
          "quote": "novel BCC-base superalloys containing Al and ETMs to form BCC-B2 coherent microstructure have been recently developed in diverse systems, which raises the concept of refractory superalloys (RSAs)",
          "table": null,
          "figure": null,
          "chunk_id": "1b6855b4033595e2:part:001"
        },
        {
          "page": 5,
          "section": null,
          "quote": "Although the creep properties of RSAs have been attracting more attention, such investigations are infrequent because the BCC-B2 coherent microstructures in most RSAs could not be stabilized at HTs.",
          "table": null,
          "figure": null,
          "chunk_id": "1b6855b4033595e2:part:002"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
